<title>TURKEY: Turkey sets 2-year inflation-indexed bond auction.</title>
<headline>Turkey sets 2-year inflation-indexed bond auction.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Turkish central bank said the Treasury would auction on Tuesday two-year, inflation plus risk premium bonds with three-month interest payments after it sold 344.5 trln lira of 399-day bonds last Tuesday.</p>
<p>The central bank has 68.1 trillion lira of reverse repo repayments due on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    Maturity    : April 2, 1999</p>
<p>    Amount	: -</p>
<p>    Coupon	: -</p>
<p>Auction date: April 1, 1997</p>
<p>Value date  : April 2, 1997</p>
<p>The Treasury's first issue of such bonds was on March 4 when it sold 18.6 trillion lira of two-year paper indexed to consumer price inflation and bearing a risk premium of 25 percent.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-275 08 75</p>
</text>
